  Code Quality Observations

  Hash Table Implementation (hash_table22.asm)

  The implementation is solid with:
  - Good scrambling for hash distribution (lines 23-31)
  - Clean separation of global vs local label hashing
  - Escape format ($01 <ptr> <ptr> .local $00) for local labels with scope verification

  Macro Expansion (asm22.asm:1637-1756)

  The macro expansion handles complex scenarios well:
  - Arguments evaluated in parent scope before pushing child scope
  - Forward references properly tracked per-pass
  - Clean recursion detection

  Forward Reference Handling (fwdref22.asm)

  Well-implemented with:
  - Pass 1: Records PC locations needing absolute mode
  - Pass 2: Consumes list entries to enforce consistent mode selection
  - Proper terminator ($FFFF) handling

  ---
  Memory Map Analysis

  $0000-$00FF  Zero page variables
  $0200-$03FF  Forward reference list (512 bytes)
  $0400-$04FF  Scope stack (256 bytes)
  $0500-$05FF  Macro argument buffer (256 bytes)
  $0600-$06FF  TOKEN buffer (256 bytes)
  $0700-$07FF  Label hash table (256 bytes)
  $2000+       Generated code (grows upward)
  ~$F000       File stack (grows downward)

  The layout is sensible. Gap between $0800 and $2000 could potentially be reclaimed if more hash table entries were needed.

